<!-- Insights › Wall display, played (design-insights §4 Playlists, CX-DEVICE; impl-insights P11): the page a wall display opens,
    the homePath of the INSIGHTS_PLAYLISTS route group (data/BossSetupData.xml), which admits this screen's render and its data
    transition and nothing else. It is the framework's wall display (Tools Dashboards/WallDisplay.xml, mr-moqui
    docs/tools/Monitoring.md "Playlists and the wall display") included at this location with its one transition, data, so
    the route group (BOSS_DEV_INS_WALL) and the display account's grant (BOSS_INS_WALL_DISPLAY) keep naming this file and
    this file's data and no Tools location: a page of its own rather than the /qapps shell, which a device may not load
    (impl-admin F285), standalone, the html mode a bare document that loads the qvt client's files and mounts the qvt render
    as an island, m-report-playlist in kiosk mode; a dashboard of the stored playlist by its index, rendered as the viewer;
    a panel's failure shown as "not available" with its text logged; any failure one fixed sentence; nothing written. The
    range is Insights' (the root's reportPolicy, which the root sets for a device's request too: now-30d to now), never the
    request's from and thru, so an unattended browser cannot make every panel query years.
    On a device the playlist is the registration's (the framework puts the registered definitionId over whatever the browser
    sends) and everything runs as the device's display account, which needs no Insights root grant (BOSS_INSIGHTS_DISPLAY opens
    this screen and its data transition alone; BOSS_INSIGHTS_READ gives the reading): a dashboard it may not read is left out and
    logged by name. A signed-in Insights user opens it too (Playlists' Play full screen), as themselves. -->
<screen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/xml-screen-3.xsd"
        default-menu-title="Wall display" default-menu-include="false" standalone="true" history="false"
        screen-theme-type-enum-id="STT_INTERNAL_QUASAR">

    <parameter name="definitionId"/>

    <transition-include name="data" location="component://tools/screen/Dashboards/WallDisplay.xml"/>

    <widgets>
        <include-screen location="component://tools/screen/Dashboards/WallDisplay.xml" share-scope="true"/>
    </widgets>
</screen>
